jax2onnx compatibility build

Based on enpasos/jax2onnx v0.8.1, distributed under Apache License 2.0.
Source: https://github.com/enpasos/jax2onnx
Base commit: 4df18bd9428da7a9e1aead47b8afceb042dfbae8

This derivative retains the legacy converter and public API for JAX 0.6.0
and Flax 0.10.7. Selected operator lowerings are adapted from jax2onnx
0.17.1 to the legacy plugin interface. It does not include all features
of jax2onnx 0.17.1.
Reference commit: 673badcbb837f1c052f888c70bc857dd23b49c16

Modifications:
- Added rsqrt lowering using Sqrt and Div, with shape and dtype metadata.
- Added general dot_general contractions using Einsum, retaining matrix fast paths.
- Preserved dynamic input dimensions when lowering broadcast_in_dim.
- Rebuilt NNX graph state inside tracing and retained nested model instances.
- Preserved native JAX batching through vmap and nested scan tracing.
- Fixed Scan/Loop result ordering, reverse iteration, and passthrough state aliases.
- Removed unused NNX state and RNG constants before conversion.
- Lifted while-loop closure values into explicit state for correct JAX data flow.
- Used native Flax math for arbitrary LayerNorm reduction axes.
- Preserved typed constants and Flax parameter promotion during export.
- Kept the caller's JAX precision configuration unchanged.
- Stored the GPT example's causal mask as a boolean array.
- Gave the float32 take test fixture an explicit parameter dtype.
- Preserved nested ONNX function instances without mutating cached JAX equations.
- Matched JAX dtype promotion in concatenation and Equinox layers.
- Isolated custom JVP and JIT subgraphs with shared conversion logic.

The public import remains jax2onnx. This compatibility distribution targets
JAX 0.6.0 and Flax 0.10.7; other JAX/Flax versions are not claimed as supported.

Project policy inference is validated with float32 compute on CPU ONNX Runtime.
BF16 numerical preservation is not claimed: the legacy converter can promote
BF16 operations to float32. GPU ONNX Runtime has not been validated.
